---
import { contactMailtoHref } from "../../config/site";
import BaseLayout from "../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Engagements — Aly Metwaly"
  description="Advisory, leadership roles, keynotes, and workshops focused on AI transformation and execution."
>
  <div class="page-vertical">
    <div class="page-image reveal-on-scroll">
      <img
        src="/images/aly-engagements.jpg"
        alt="Working with leaders and organizations"
        loading="lazy"
      />
    </div>

    <div class="page-content">
      <div class="kicker reveal-on-scroll">
        <span class="kicker-dot"></span>
        Advisory · Leadership roles · Keynotes · Workshops
      </div>

      <h1 class="reveal-on-scroll">How I work with leaders and organizations</h1>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        I work with organizations that are serious about moving AI from experimentation
        to measurable impact. The form of our collaboration can vary, but the focus
        remains constant: clarity of intent, operating model design, and execution
        that holds up under real enterprise constraints.
      </p>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Advisory &amp; leadership roles</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        I engage with leadership teams in advisory, fractional, or full-time roles
        where AI transformation requires sustained ownership rather than isolated
        initiatives.
      </p>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Designing AI operating models that scale beyond pilots</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Clarifying governance, decision rights, and accountability</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Aligning AI ambition with organizational reality</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Translating strategy into execution mechanisms</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Keynotes &amp; leadership sessions</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        I deliver keynotes and leadership sessions for executive and senior audiences
        who want clarity rather than hype. These sessions focus on framing AI as an
        operating model challenge, not a tooling exercise.
      </p>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Audiences typically leave with sharper mental models, clearer language,
        and a more grounded basis for decision-making.
      </p>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Workshops</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        Workshops are designed to turn intent into action. They are hands-on,
        context-aware, and grounded in enterprise realities.
      </p>

      <ul class="plain-list">
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">AI adoption in real workflows</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Operating model and governance design</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Metrics, ownership, and accountability</li>
        <li class="reveal-on-scroll">Moving from pilots to repeatable execution</li>
      </ul>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Who this is for</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        My work is most relevant for leaders operating in large or complex
        organizations where scale, cost, governance, and risk matter.
      </p>

      <h2 class="reveal-on-scroll">Start a conversation</h2>

      <p class="reveal-on-scroll">
        I am open to discussions around leadership roles, advisory engagements,
        keynotes, and workshops.
      </p>

      <div class="actions reveal-on-scroll">
        <a class="button primary" href={contactMailtoHref}>
          Start a conversation
        </a>
        <a class="button" href="/about">About</a>
        <a class="button" href="/work">See work</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
